<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cirta</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Constantina</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cirta was the capital of the Numidian kingdom, on a rocky plateau above the Rhumel gorge in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a>. It was a royal seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syphax">Syphax</a> and then of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masinissa">Masinissa</a> and his heirs, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurtha">Jugurtha</a>'s massacre of Italian traders there in 112 BCE led to war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. Rebuilt by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine the Great</a>, it took the name Constantina, today Constantine.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cirta.jpg" alt="Cirta" width="320" height="502" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tangopaso · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mosaique_de_sol_avec_le_triomphe_de_Neptune_et_son_%C3%A9pouse_Amphitrite_(Louvre,_Ma_1880)1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
